AUTHOR BIOGRAPHIES
Dr. Emily Slade is an assistant professor at the University of Kentucky and the founder and director of the Biostatistics Consulting and Inter
disciplinary Research Collaboration Lab (Biostat CIRCL). Her research focuses on effective training and integration of biostatisticians on bio
medical research teams.
Sarah Jane K. Robbins is a biostatistician in the Biostatistics Consulting and Interdisciplinary Research Collaboration Lab (Biostat CIRCL) at
the University of Kentucky. She is a member of several interdisciplinary research teams across the university's campus.
Kristen J. McQuerry is an associate professor of Biostatistics and member of the Biostatistics Consulting and Interdisciplinary Research Col
laboration Lab (Biostat CIRCL) at the University of Kentucky. Her research focuses on developing the next generation for biostatisticians
through community outreach.
Anthony A. Mangino is a biomedical data scientist in the Biostatistics Consulting and Interdisciplinary Research Collaboration Lab (Biostat
CIRCL) at the University of Kentucky. He collaborates with numerous research teams across campus and studies methods for using generative
models to improve conventional analytic frameworks.
